      "title": "The Threefold Witness (1 John 5:6-8)",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "id": "block_3",
          "text": "The text identifies Jesus Christ as the one who came through water and blood. The Spirit bears witness to this reality. The longer form of verses 7-8 known as the Comma Johanneum (mentioning heavenly witnesses) is later than the earliest recoverable Greek manuscripts and represents a secondary expansion of the original text.",
